  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1139 PM CDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nAfter a chilly start to the morning on Saturday, temperatures will \nslowly warm into the low to mid 60s by afternoon. These highs are 15 \nto 20 degrees below seasonal normals. Good radiational cooling \nconditions are forecast Sunday morning, as winds become light and \nvariable and skies remain clear. Overnight lows are forecast to drop \ninto the upper 30s to lower 40s across most of the area. Low-lying \nareas and river valleys may drop into the mid 30s. A light frost is \npossible across the area, especially across low-lying areas where \nthe coldest temperatures are forecast. Another cool day is forecast \non Sunday with highs in 60s to near 70. Overnight lows will be in \nthe mid to upper 40s. \n\nA steady warm up is then forecast through next week. Highs on Monday \nwill be back into the 70s, with highs on Tuesday approaching 80. \nUpper level ridging then develops across the area for the second \nhalf of the work week, resulting in highs well into the 80s. Dry \nconditions are forecast to continue through much of the work week.",
